The Bible has 66 books — don't keep cycling through Psalm 91 / Philippians 4:6-7 / Isaiah 41:10. Branch into less-quoted passages that fit this prayer's specific theme. Examples of underused but powerful passages: Lamentations 3:22-24 (mercies new every morning), Zephaniah 3:17 (God rejoices over you with singing), Habakkuk 3:17-19 (joy in scarcity), 2 Corinthians 12:9 (grace sufficient in weakness), Hebrews 4:14-16 (approach the throne of grace), 1 Peter 5:7 (cast your anxieties), Romans 8:28 (all things work for good), James 1:2-4 (count it joy), Isaiah 43:1-3 (passing through waters), Psalm 34:18 (close to the brokenhearted), Psalm 139:7-12 (nowhere from His presence).
